<p>Use this menu to make settings for printing a single document page over 
 multiple sheets.</p>
<p>Available functions differ depending on the printer or printer driver you are using.</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you are using, this function may not be available.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="default" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Restore Defaults</span></p>
<p>Restores the settings on this menu to the default settings.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="poster" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Poster:</span></p>
<p>Prints a single document page printed over multiple sheets.</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/RPCS/idh_how_poster">Splitting the Document Image across 
 Multiple Sheets (Poster)</a></p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="pamphlet" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Pamphlet:</span></p>
<p>Arranges eight pages on one sheet using a layout suitable for pamphlets.<br/>
Cut and fold the sheet according to the lines to make a pamphlet.</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/RPCS/idh_how_pamphlet">Printing Eight Pages on a Sheet 
 for Making Pamphlets</a></p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Draw Border</span></p>
<p>Select the check box to have document pages delineated by a dotted line.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="speed" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Imposition (Speed):</span></p>
<p>Prints two pages of a document side by side on one sheet of paper. The 
 sheet can then be cut in half and stacked in the specified order (left 
 to right/right to left/top to bottom) to make one copy of a document. 
 </p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/RPCS/IDH_HOW_IMPOSITION">Printing a Document with Imposition 
 Methods</a></p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="double" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Imposition (Double):</span></p>
<p>Prints two copies of a document side by side on one sheet of paper. 
 The sheet can then be cut in half to make two copies of a document.</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/RPCS/IDH_HOW_IMPOSITION">Printing a Document with Imposition 
 Methods</a></p>
